A||||4||XDrewX||how do i know if p.o. did a/c conversion?||||5||
Z||000000||XDrewX||06-14-2001||09:49 PM||||my 87 gt has 60k on it, i need to recharge my a/c, but i don't know if it has already been converted ? <BR>is there any tell tale sign ?<P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||skitime||06-14-2001||09:56 PM||||The fitting used to fill it are different. <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||XDrewX||06-14-2001||10:06 PM||||thats what i thought<P>thanks<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||06-14-2001||10:14 PM||||If you have screw on fittings it is still R12. If they are QuikConnect, they are R134a.<P>And if they put the caps on, R12 caps are black, R134a are red and blue.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-14-2001||11:26 PM||||Well... that's what's suposed to happen.... doesn't mean it did and therefor you can't go by the fittings.<P>Any competant AC shop will have a refrigerant analyzer. this unit will tell you just what is in there. This is especially critical with the use of illegal hydrocarbon containing/based refrigerant being all to common.<P>If you want to know what refrigerants are EPA rated you can look it up on the EPA web site. Refrigerants containing hydrocarbon are banned in motor vehicles in most jurisdictions.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.epa.gov/ozone/title6/609/choice.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.epa.gov/ozone/title6/609/choice.html</A> ||||reg||1
